    10	`archive/multi-catfish-pre-v03-2026-08-31/` is historical and must not be used
    11	to launch or explain V0.3.
    12	
    13	For the paper main text and main presentation, use
    14	`MULTI-CATFISH-MCRL-V03-PRESENTATION-LAYER-2026-08-31.md`. It compresses this
    15	complete specification into one intervention, three views, three route-local
    16	estimators, and one deployed action. Its omissions are authoring choices only;
    17	this full specification remains the reproducibility and implementation
    18	authority.
    19	
    20	## 1. Objective and invariant
    21	
    22	The only scientific endpoint is canonical ratio-of-sums energy efficiency:
    23	
    24	\[
    25	\eta^N=\frac{\mathcal B}{\mathcal E},\qquad
    26	\mathcal B=\sum_t\sum_{u\in\mathcal U}R_u(t)\Delta t,\qquad
    27	\mathcal E=\sum_tP^N(t)\Delta t.
    28	\]
    29	
    30	The old directions of `r2` and `r3` are not objectives. V0.3 uses three
    31	training-time views of how one focal action can change the same final EE. A
    32	route survives only when its informed source improves held-out Main-only EE
    33	over its equal-budget neutral replacement without violating the service guard.
    34	
    35	## 2. Exactly three Q functions
    36	
    37	V0.3 contains exactly three independent online Q functions:
    38	
    39	```text
    40	C1 source route -> Q1(s_u(t),a) --\
    41	C2 source route -> Q2(s_u(t),a) ----> Phi_u=Q1+Q2+Q3 -> one masked argmax
    42	C3 source route -> Q3(s_u(t),a) --/
    43	```
    44	
    45	- Each Q has independent parameters and its own optimizer; no trainable trunk
    46	  is shared.
    47	- Pilot 1 is zero-bootstrap pairwise regression. It has no target networks.
    48	- A route-\(j\) row may change only \(Q_j\).
    49	- Catfish routes generate and schedule training comparisons; they are not
    50	  three extra networks. A six-Q interpretation is invalid for V0.3.
    51	- Legacy Bellman replay, old `r1/r2/r3` targets, old target networks, and old
    52	  checkpoints are unit-incompatible and fail closed.
    53	
    54	## 3. One matched intervention, three non-overlapping targets
    55	
    56	Freeze one TRAIN-only multiplier before Catfish outcomes are inspected:
    57	
    58	\[
    59	\lambda_0=\frac{\mathcal B_0^M}{\mathcal E_0^M},\qquad
    60	g_k=\Delta\mathcal B_k-\lambda_0\Delta\mathcal E_k,
    61	\]
    62	\[
    63	\Delta\mathcal B_k=\Delta t\sum_{i\in\mathcal U}
    64	[R_i^C(k)-R_i^M(k)],\qquad
    65	\Delta\mathcal E_k=\Delta t[P_C^N(k)-P_M^N(k)].
    66	\]
    67	
    68	At an anchor, candidate branch \(C\) and reference branch \(M\) initially
    69	differ only in focal user \(u\)'s physical action.
    70	
    71	### C1: focal now
    72	
    73	\[
    74	\zeta_{1,u}=\Delta t[R_u^C(0)-R_u^M(0)]
    75	-\lambda_0\Delta t[P_C^N(0)-P_M^N(0)].
    76	\]
    77	
    78	C1 assigns the complete opening-step energy difference to the only mover. It
    79	is the direct immediate net-surplus path.
    80	
    81	### C3: others now
    82	
    83	\[
    84	\zeta_{3,u}=\Delta t\sum_{i\in\mathcal U\setminus\{u\}}
    85	[R_i^C(0)-R_i^M(0)].
    86	\]
    87	
    88	C3 captures the focal action's immediate non-focal rate externality through
    89	load, bandwidth sharing, co-channel interference, and shared activation.
    90	Opening energy is not repeated here because it already belongs to C1.
    91	
    92	### C2: everyone later
    93	
    94	\[
    95	\zeta_{2,u}=\sum_{k=1}^{H^c-1}\left\{
    96	\Delta t\sum_{i\in\mathcal U}[R_i^C(k)-R_i^M(k)]
    97	-\lambda_0\Delta t[P_C^N(k)-P_M^N(k)]
    98	\right\}.
    99	\]
   100	
   101	C2 captures downstream effects of holding, switching, release, recurrence
   102	power, interruption, and later availability. Pilot 1 uses \(H^c=4\), so offsets
   103	1, 2, and 3 all belong to C2. The V0.3B C2 amendment holds the opening
   104	candidate only while it remains uniquely legal in the candidate branch. At
   105	the first support-expiry offset, it releases monotonically to complete
   106	contemporaneous branch-local Main; it never looks ahead or reacquires the held
   107	key.
   108	
   109	The exact bookkeeping identity is
   110	
   111	\[
   112	\zeta_{1,u}+\zeta_{3,u}+\zeta_{2,u}=\sum_{k=0}^{H^c-1}g_k.
   113	\]
   114	
   115	It proves non-overlap, not learnability or efficacy.
   116	
   117	## 4. The three Catfish source mechanisms
   118	
   119	All informed and neutral schedules are sealed from predecision information
   120	before targets are evaluated. Positive, zero, negative, and all-dark complete
   121	outcomes are retained. Opening support failure is right-censored and reported,
   122	never replaced or imputed. A downstream C2 hold expiry is instead a sealed
   123	reactive release event and remains in the complete trace.
   124	
   125	| Route | Informed mechanism | Equal-budget neutral replacement | Update |
   126	|---|---|---|---|
   127	| C1 Energy-Frontier | RIS-lineage dull-rollout EXP schedules lower-frontier anchors and users, then compares every sealed legal alternative with frozen Main | uniformly sample eligible Main anchors, users with at least two legal actions, and legal alternatives | only \(Q_1\) with \(\zeta_1\) |
   128	| C2 Temporal-Fork | at a departure anchor, compare Main with `hold-or-max-lagged-SINR-rival`; if Main leaves a valid incumbent, hold it, otherwise choose the legal non-Main rival with maximum predecision `candidate_sinr` evaluated against the previous radiating set, with physical-ID then action-ID tie breaks; hold while legal, then release once to contemporaneous branch-local Main | uniformly sample an eligible anchor and focal user under the same \(H^c\), release grammar, and oracle budget | only \(Q_2\) with \(\zeta_2\) |
   129	| C3 Spatial-Externality | use lagged competitive-load anchors, choose users spanning multiple physical alternatives, and enumerate sealed unilateral legal actions | uniformly sample eligible anchors/users and the same number of legal alternatives | only \(Q_3\) with \(\zeta_3\) |
   130	
   131	### C1 EXP/ACRM lineage
   132	
   133	V0.3 preserves the two ideas without changing output units:
   134	
   135	1. **EXP** is informed source construction and stratification on disjoint
   136	   TRAIN-only dull-rollout data.
   137	2. **ACRM** is the reference-anchored candidate-versus-Main comparison inside
   138	   the C1 pairwise advantage. It is a unit-safe adaptation of competitive
   139	   learning, not an additive shaped reward.
   140	
   141	The superseded formula that added an ACRM reward directly to a Bellman target is
   142	not used: it would make \(Q_1\) incomparable with \(Q_2\) and \(Q_3\). A later
   143	C1 component study may compare EXP-only and EXP-plus-source-priority variants,
   144	but no component may alter the canonical EE formula or the deployed Q unit.
   145	
   146	## 5. Phase-I data products
   147	
   148	V0.3 separates cheap opening comparisons, expensive temporal comparisons, and
   149	identity auditing:
   150	
   151	| Set | Contents | Gradient use |
   152	|---|---|---|
   153	| \(D^o\) | offset-0 matched pair; raw per-user rates and system power; both \(\zeta_1\) and \(\zeta_3\); source tag C1 or C3 | source C1 updates only \(Q_1\); source C3 updates only \(Q_3\) |
   154	| \(D^t\) | full \(H^c\)-offset C2 pair; raw trace; \(\zeta_2\); release offset/reason; held-key match counts; policy and random-field version | updates only \(Q_2\) |
   155	| \(D^a\) | held-out full trace with all \(\zeta_1,\zeta_2,\zeta_3,g_k\) | never enters a loss; identity/distinctness/deployment audit only |
   156	
   157	Every row binds at least:
   158	
   159	```text
   160	row id, source j, data-set version, seed, anchor and focal user,
   161	reference/candidate physical keys and action slots, stored decision mask,
   162	observation-schema version, policy/checkpoint digest, lambda/kappa hex,
   163	horizon and random-field version, C2 release offset/reason when applicable,
   164	raw rate/power trace, target(s),
   165	completion/censor outcome, and trace digests
   166	```
   167	
   168	The source quota, quantile, and exact observation dimension remain preregistration
   169	parameters. They may change before the first claim-bearing run without changing
   170	the algorithm diagram.
   171	
   172	## 6. Pairwise learning
   173	
   174	Use one shared positive scale:
   175	
   176	\[
   177	\widetilde\zeta_{j,u}=\frac{\zeta_{j,u}}{\kappa},\qquad
   178	\kappa=\frac{\mathcal B_0^M}{n_0}.
   179	\]
   180	
   181	For a route-\(j\) comparison:
   182	
   183	\[
   184	\ell_j=w_j\left(
   185	[Q_j(s_u(t),a_u^C(t))-Q_j(s_u(t),a_u^M(t))
   186	-\widetilde\zeta_{j,u}]^2
   187	+\beta Q_j(s_u(t),a_u^M(t))^2
   188	\right).
   189	\]
   190	
   191	- \(w_j\) normalizes loss noise only; deployment weights remain one.
   192	- \(\beta\) is a numerical gauge, provisionally 0.1 and frozen before the
   193	  claim-bearing run.
   194	- No Bellman bootstrap, target net, voting loss, redundant sum loss, or
   195	  cross-route gradient is permitted.
   196	- Swap of reference/candidate reverses the target sign; an identical pair has
   197	  zero target.
   198	
   199	## 7. Deployment
   200	
   201	Only Main executes:
   202	
   203	\[
   204	\Phi_u(t,a)=Q_1(s_u(t),a)+Q_2(s_u(t),a)+Q_3(s_u(t),a),\qquad
   205	a_u^\star(t)=\arg\max_{a\in A_u(t)}\Phi_u(t,a).
   206	\]
   207	
   208	There is no Catfish action at evaluation time, no auction, coordinator,
   209	matching, voting, joint decoder, or post-training override.
   210	
   211	## 8. Initial ablation matrix
   212	
   213	Every V0.3 pairwise arm retains the same three-Q topology. Replacing a Catfish
   214	means replacing its informed source with its equal-budget neutral source; it
   215	does not delete the Q head or reallocate its gradient budget.
   216	
   217	| Arm | C1 source | C2 source | C3 source | Purpose |
   218	|---|---|---|---|---|
   219	| \(N000\) | neutral | neutral | neutral | pairwise-learning control |
   220	| \(F111\) | informed | informed | informed | full Multi-Catfish MCRL |
   221	| \(A011\) | neutral | informed | informed | C1 conditional contribution |
   222	| \(A101\) | informed | neutral | informed | C2 conditional contribution |
   223	| \(A110\) | informed | informed | neutral | C3 conditional contribution |
   224	
   225	The original frozen MODQN policy \(M0\) is evaluated as a separate external
   226	baseline under the same fresh seeds and canonical ratio-of-sums EE. It is not
   227	renamed \(N000\). Singleton arms may be added later for full interaction
   228	estimation, but they do not block the first full/leave-one-out trend screen.
   229	
   230	## 9. Evaluation and survival rule
   231	
   232	For each fresh evaluation seed report:
   233	
   234	\[
   235	\eta^N=\frac{\sum_t\sum_{u\in\mathcal U}R_u(t)\Delta t}
   236	{\sum_tP^N(t)\Delta t},
   237	\]
   238	
   239	plus total bits \(\mathcal B\), total energy \(\mathcal E\), served fraction, and outage. Reward
   240	means are not substitutes for this endpoint.
   241	
   242	- Full mechanism screen: \(F111>N000\) and \(F111>M0\).
   243	- C1 contribution: \(F111>A011\).
   244	- C2 contribution: \(F111>A101\).
   245	- C3 contribution: \(F111>A110\).
   246	- Each comparison is paired by training/evaluation seeds and must satisfy the
   247	  preregistered service guard.
   248	
   249	A failed route is reported as a failed mechanism. It is not rescued by
   250	improving its private target, by changing thresholds after reveal, or by a
   251	post-training coordinator.
   252	
   253	## 10. Minimal algorithm
   254	
   255	```text
   256	freeze TRAIN-only lambda0, kappa, source rules, seeds, and schemas
   257	build D^o from sealed C1/C3 opening pairs
   258	build D^t from sealed C2 H^c-step temporal pairs under keyed common fading
   259	build held-out D^a and verify the full identity
   260	
   261	initialize three independent online functions Q1, Q2, Q3
   262	for each scheduled source update:
   263	    read one version-compatible pair batch from route j
   264	    compute paper target zeta_j/kappa
   265	    update only Qj with the pairwise advantage and gauge loss
   266	    reject any legacy replay/checkpoint/target schema
   267	
   268	at evaluation/deployment:
   269	    compute Q1+Q2+Q3
   270	    execute one safe masked argmax
   150	This predicate is not a promise of lower system power or higher EE. Moving load
   151	can change bandwidth sharing, rate, feasibility, beam activation, and power,
   152	so the indirect EE effect remains an empirical singleton and ablation result.
   153	
   154	## 7. Counterfactual evidence is audit-only
   155	
   156	Four-offset counterfactual replay remains permitted for bounded Stage-0
   157	measurement and scientific audit, never for online admission. In particular,
   158	the completed 9-focal by 8-candidate TLE scan showed that 9 of 72 candidates
   159	strictly improved both hold-window and full-window system `r2`, but only two
   160	candidates survived the older full certificate and they occurred at different
   161	focals. That receipt killed the V0.1 per-anchor certificate as a scalable
   162	runtime mechanism; it did not select the V0.2 predicates or the support floor.
