     2	
     3	**The network never changes.**  It stays a flat 28-output MLP with hidden
     4	layers ``(100, 50, 50)`` and ``tanh``.  Everything in this module is
     5	environment-side bookkeeping (SDD §4A preamble, §3.3).
     6	
     7	Index layout (§4A.1)::
     8	
     9	    a = 7·l + j        l ∈ {0,1,2,3} satellite slot,  j ∈ {0,…,6} beam slot
    10	
    11	The four state blocks use the same ``(l, j)`` order, so state and action are
    12	aligned by construction.
    13	
    14	The load-bearing rule of the whole module (§4A.4)::
    15	
    16	    handover is decided from the REALISED ASSOCIATION (norad_id, cell_id),
    17	    never from the action index
    18	
    19	Comparing indices fails two ways that no assertion would catch: a forced
    20	handover after the incumbent loses eligibility keeps index 0 and reads as
    21	"no handover" (false negative), and returning to the same satellite after it
    22	becomes the incumbent changes the index and reads as a handover that never
    23	happened (false positive).  Tests T1 and T2 pin both.
