/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:110:- **D-MIN-2 (suspicious result, unexplained). `S_UNI` is exactly degenerate with `BASELINE`.** Pooled EE for `S_UNI` equals `BASELINE` to the last digit (16 987 632 bits/J) at every one of the 5 anchors. Under the 5 s pilot `compute_budget_s`, `_s_uni_select` returned the carrier base unchanged, i.e. it found no accepted unilateral improvement at all. The `FULL-vs-S_UNI` contrast below is therefore **not** a comparison against exhaustive unilateral improvement; per contract v1.2 item 6 it is at best a budget-limited operational comparator, and in this run it is an empty one. Do not read it as evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:112:- **D-MIN-4 (internal inconsistency). `V_CA` is large and negative while `FULL` pooled EE is the highest of all arms.** Net `V_CA` is -1.365e11 bit-equivalents (bits -1.222e10, -eta*energy -3.373e10, Phi -9.054e10) against the additive selector, yet `FULL` pooled EE (3.425e7) exceeds `DROP_C3` (2.352e7), `S0` (1.759e7) and `BASELINE` (1.699e7). Either the `V_CA` reference (the additive selector) or the pooled-EE aggregation is not measuring what the schema intends. **This must be resolved before any V_CA number is reported at scale.**
